import {practicePack,practicePackVersion} from './practice-pack.mjs';
import {escapeHTML as e} from './core.mjs';
export const resourcesHTML=`<div class="eyebrow">NEPOCORE / FREE TEACHING RESOURCES</div><h1>Free math practice pack with answer keys</h1><p>Three original arithmetic worksheets, 20 questions each, with a separate answer page after every activity. Print a ready-made A4 pack or make a fresh version in Worksheet Studio.</p><p><a class="btn primary" href="./assets/resources/nepocore-math-practice-pack-${practicePackVersion}.pdf" download>Download the 6-page practice pack ↓</a> <a class="btn secondary" href="./worksheets/">Create a custom worksheet ↗</a></p><p>Published 5 November 2026 by Nepocore. Designed for home and classroom practice; no curriculum alignment, assessment result or learning guarantee is claimed.</p><h2>What is inside?</h2><div class="article-table"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Activity</th><th scope="col">Question page</th><th scope="col">Answer page</th></tr></thead><tbody>${practicePack.map((set,i)=>`<tr><td>${e(set.title)}</td><td>${i*2+1}</td><td>${i*2+2}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><h2>A simple way to use the pack</h2><ol><li>Choose one activity that matches a skill the learner has already met.</li><li>Print only pages 1, 3 and 5 for question sheets. Keep pages 2, 4 and 6 for checking.</li><li>Allow working time and ask the learner to explain a method for a few answers.</li><li>Review errors together, then generate another short practice sheet if useful.</li></ol><p>The PDF uses A4 pages, 210 × 297 mm. Match the printer paper setting and inspect a single-page preview before printing a batch. If using US Letter, check the printer’s fit setting and margins. See the <a href="./worksheets/guides/print-worksheets-a4-letter/">A4 and Letter printing guide</a>.</p><h2>Read the questions and answers as text</h2><p>The same content is available below for readers who prefer HTML. Expand an activity to check its questions, or <a href="./assets/resources/practice-pack.json">download the structured problem data</a>.</p>${practicePack.map(set=>`<details><summary>${e(set.title)} — 20 questions and answers</summary><div class="article-table"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">No.</th><th scope="col">Question</th><th scope="col">Answer</th></tr></thead><tbody>${set.problems.map((p,i)=>`<tr><td>${i+1}</td><td>${p.a} ${p.op==='multiply'?'×':p.op==='add'?'+':'−'} ${p.b}</td><td>${p.answer}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div></details>`).join('')}<h2>Make it fit the next lesson</h2><p>The sample pack is a fixed set of examples. <a href="./worksheets/">Worksheet Studio</a> can generate new math questions, change difficulty and question count, choose A4 or US Letter, and include separate answer keys. For a different activity, make a <a href="./worksheets/spelling-worksheet-maker/">spelling worksheet from your own words</a> or a <a href="./worksheets/word-search-generator/">custom word-search puzzle</a>.</p><p>For planning help, read <a href="./worksheets/guides/build-a-week-of-math-practice/">how to build a manageable week of practice</a>. For understanding calculations, try the <a href="./tools/calculator/">scientific calculator</a> and its <a href="./blog/scientific-calculator-degrees-sin-log-factorial/">worked degree-mode examples</a>.</p><h2>Share a useful resource</h2><p>You may print and share these original sample sheets for home or classroom practice without an account or payment. A source mention is welcome but optional. Link to this resource page when you want readers to find the current pack, text version and custom generator together.</p><p>Suggested reference: <strong>Nepocore math practice pack — three printable worksheets with separate answer keys.</strong></p><p>Questions or a correction? <a href="./contact/">Contact Nepocore</a>. Read our <a href="./editorial-policy/">editorial and corrections policy</a> for how instructions and worked examples are prepared.</p>`;
